    "If the evaluator flags a lot of abrupt endings, it might indicate the model struggles with follow-up questions, even if it performs well on straightforward queries.",
    "Sampling in online evaluation is **stratified and intentional**, focusing on conversations most likely to reveal flaws because those are the ones that matter most for real-world performance.",
    "The rest of the flow—evaluator setup, metric aggregation, and alerting—is the machinery that turns these samples into actionable insights."
